  "note": "CLC maps at 25 ha minimum mapping unit: a context layer for cities that does not resolve single parks, streets or squares. Urban fabric has no use split in CLC; both urban-fabric classes are drawn as residential_area (the Urban Atlas manual defines urban fabric as predominantly residential and the INSPIRE Land Use guideline maps it to HILUCS 5 ResidentialUse); 111 also covers city centres, remap it to mixed_use_area to set cores apart. 141 and 142 are pink in the official legend, not green. Entries 11-52 and 1-5 are the level-2 and level-1 groups, keyed by the leading digits of the level-3 code for the prefix fallback; they have no legend colour. Raster editions can store a legend index instead of the three-digit code: translate to the code first, otherwise small index values hit the group entries. Change layers carry two code columns: pass column= explicitly. Attribute maes is the official CLC to MAES ecosystem-type correspondence (BISE).",
